# Naming and style (modern_exchng_cpp)

Apply this to new and edited code. It overrides Google C++ Style. This rule is complete for naming and braces; do not open a doc for a routine edit.

| Kind | Convention | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| Functions | PascalCase | `SubmitLimitOrder`, `CancelOrder` |
| Variables | snake_case | `order_id`, `price_level` |
| Classes / structs / types | PascalCase | `OrderNode`, `PriceLevel`, `Book` |
| Class members | snake_case + trailing `_` | `order_id_` |
| Struct members | snake_case, no `_` suffix | `order_id` |
| Constants / `constexpr` | `k` + PascalCase | `kMaxOrders`, `kInvalid` |
| Enumerators | `k` + PascalCase | `Side::kBuy` |
| Namespaces | lowercase, underscores if needed | `order_book` |
| Template parameters | PascalCase | `TNode` |
| Macros | avoid; if required, `ALL_CAPS` | `MAX_ORDERS` |

- **Braces:** Allman — `{` and `}` on their own line for every block, including `if` / `else` / `while` / `for`.
- **Design:** composition over inheritance.
- **Files:** lowercase with underscores or dashes; `.hpp` / `.cpp` to match existing files.
- **Legacy names:** leave `INVALID` and `Side::Buy` / `Side::Sell` in `book.hpp` unless the user asks to rename them. New code uses `kInvalid`, `Side::kBuy`, `Side::kSell`.
